[Music]  the existence of home court advantage is  one of the most  durable empirical patterns in all of  sports however  the relative importance of mechanisms  explaining its strength  such as fan attendance still remains a  mystery  capacity restrictions during the  2020-2021 nba season  allow us an opportunity to identify the  effect of crowds on home court advantage  over the course of 440 games played in  front of empty arenas during the season  the home team won by an average of 0.39  points  this is in stark contrast to the 2.13  average point margin  during the more than 500 games played  with crowds  this is a similar effect to starting an  all-star  over an average nba player in short  the data say exactly what any passionate  fan  already knows fans matter  so next time your favorite basketball  team geeks out at one point when at home  you have proof that your spirited  cheering really did make the difference  between winning  and losing how important do you think  fans are for home court advantage  let us know in our poll also let us know  what other topics you'd like our  scholars to cover in 60 seconds  and be sure to like and subscribe for  more research and videos  from aei

